 // bt3SwapHook) the back buffer is copied on the GPU into an image the native renderer's Vulkan device owns and GL imports
 // (GL_EXT_memory_object), GL signals an exported semaphore, and Vulkan copies the image into a swapchain image and presents
-// it. The swapchain lives on a child window covering the GL window's client area (Vulkan cannot present to a window GL has
-// claimed); the child is disabled and transparent to hit-testing, so the mouse and keyboard still reach the GL window and
-// SDL. GL never swaps again, so the swapchain's present mode paces the loop: FIFO (vsync, the default), or mailbox /
+// it. The swapchain presents to the game's own window: GL draws into it but never swaps it again once Vulkan has presented
+// (a frame that cannot be presented -- minimised, being resized -- is skipped, never handed back to GL), so it works in
+// exclusive fullscreen too. (It used to live on a child window over the GL one: in exclusive fullscreen Windows shows only
+// the top-level window, which no longer swapped, and the screen was black.) A driver that refuses a Vulkan swapchain on a
+// window GL has drawn into fails at the first one, and the window stays GL's. The swapchain's present mode paces the
+// loop: FIFO (vsync, the default), or mailbox /
 // immediate (PS2X_SEAMVK_VKPRESENT_MODE) for an uncapped display. A presentation that ends in Vulkan is also what driver
